quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  68,16,Now We shall brand him on the snout.
  68,17,"Surely, We will try them (the inhabitants of Mecca in the same way) as We tried (in Yemen) the owners of the garden when they swore that they would surely pluck its fruit the next morning."
  68,18,And they did not make any exception (saying ‘if Allah wills’ or for the share of the orphans).
  68,19,"So a whirl (of disaster) from your Lord went round (that garden during the night) whilst they were asleep,"
  68,20,"So, that (waving fruit-laden garden) became a harvested field in the morning."
  68,21,"Then as the day dawned, they started calling out one another:"
  68,22,‘Leave early for your tilth if you want to pick the fruit.’
  68,23,So they set off whispering to one another:
  68,24,‘Do not let any pauper come near you in the garden today.’
  68,25,"And early in the morning they left, (feeling) quite competent to execute their plan (of getting the yield and depriving the poor of their share)."
  68,26,"Then when they saw that (ruined garden), they said: ‘We must have lost our way; (this is not our garden).’"
  68,27,"(But when they saw it cautiously, they cried: ‘Oh no!) We have been deprived indeed.’"
  68,28,"One of them, wise and inclined to the balanced judgment, said: ‘Did I not say to you: Why do you not glorify and remember Allah?’"
  68,29,"(Then) they said: ‘Our Lord is Holy. Surely, it is we who were the wrongdoers.’"
  68,30,"So, blaming and maligning, they turned to one another."
  68,31,They said: ‘Woe to us! No doubt it is we who were disobedient and rebellious.
  68,32,"We hope that our Lord may give us something better than this in exchange. Verily, we turn to our Lord.’"
  68,33,"Such is the punishment. And truly, the torment of the Hereafter is far greater (than this). Would that they only knew!"
  68,34,"Surely, for the Godfearing there are Gardens of Bliss with their Lord."
  68,35,Shall We (deprive) the obedient like the disobedient?
  68,36,What is the matter with you? How do you make a judgment?
  68,37,"Do you have any Book with you in which you read (this),"
  68,38,That it contains all that you like?
  68,39,Or have you any (such) firm covenants from Us as will subsist till the Day of Resurrection (by means of which We are bound) that you will be provided with whatever you shall decide (for yourselves)?
  68,40,Ask them which of them will vouch for such (a baseless assertion)!
  68,41,Or do they have any partners (as well)? Then they should bring their partners if they are truthful.
  68,42,"The Day when the ‘shin’ (i.e., the terrifying fierceness of the Hour of Rising) will be laid bare, and (the disobedient) people will be called to prostrate themselves, but they will not be able to do so (i.e., to prostrate themselves)."
